<title>POLAND: Petrobank to choose new supervisory board.</title>
<headline>Petrobank to choose new supervisory board.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders of Polish bank Petrobank SA will vote on the extraordinary shareholders' meeting on January 13 to pick a new supervisory board and change the bank's name, the bank said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said its new name will be LG Petro Bank SA.</p>
<p>It said shareholders would vote on dismissing the old supervisory board and choosing its new members.</p>
<p>On Wednesday LG Investment Holdings BV, a subsidiary of South Korea's LG Group which holds more than 50 percent of Poland's Petrobank SA, announced a public tender offer for the bank's remaining common shares.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
